  "term": "Dilantin",
  "definition": "Dilantin is phenytoin sodium, a non-sedating antiepileptic drug used to reduce seizure activity. It works by helping stabilize neurons in the motor cortex and limiting repeated nerve firing and spread of seizure signals.",
